  "text": "To solve this problem, we need to find the largest base \\( b \\) such that the sum of the digits of \\( 12^5 \\) in base \\( b \\) is not equal to 41. Here's a step-by-step approach:\n\n### Step 1: Calculate \\( 12^5 \\) in Base 10\nFirst, compute \\( 12^5 \\) in base 10:\n\\[\n12^5 = 12 \\times 12 \\times 12 \\times 12 \\times 12 = 248832\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Understand Base \\( b \\) Representation\nIn base \\( b \\), the number \\( 12 \\) represents:\n\\[\n1 \\times b + 2 = b + 2\n\\]\nThus, \\( 12^5 \\) in base \\( b \\) is:\n\\[\n(b + 2)^5\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Compute \\( (b + 2)^5 \\)\nExpand \\( (b + 2)^5 \\):\n\\[\n(b + 2)^5 = b^5 + 10b^4 + 40b^3 + 80b^2 + 80b + 32\n\\]\n\n### Step 4: Sum of Digits in Base \\( b \\)\nThe sum of the digits of \\( (b + 2)^5 \\) in base \\( b \\) is:\n\\[\nb^4 + 10b^3 + 40b^2 + 80b + 80\n\\]\nWe want this sum to be **not** equal to 41:\n\\[\nb^4 + 10b^3 + 40b^2 + 80b + 80 \\neq 41\n\\]\n\n### Step 5: Solve for \\( b \\)\nWe need to find the largest \\( b \\) such that the above inequality holds. Let's test values of \\( b \\) starting from \\( b = 10 \\) (since \\( b \\) must be greater than the digits in \\( 12^5 \\)):\n\n- **\\( b = 10 \\):**\n  \\[\n  10^4 + 10 \\times 10^3 + 40 \\times 10^2 + 80 \\times 10 + 80 = 10000 + 10000 + 4000 + 800 + 80 = 24880\n  \\]\n  This is not equal to 41.\n\n- **\\( b = 11 \\):**\n  \\[\n  11^4 + 10 \\times 11^3 + 40 \\times 11^2 + 80 \\times 11 + 80 = 14641 + 13310 + 4840 + 880 + 80 = 33751\n  \\]\n  This is not equal to 41.\n\n- **\\( b = 12 \\):**\n  \\[\n  12^4 + 10 \\times 12^3 + 40 \\times 12^2 + 80 \\times 12 + 80 = 20736 + 17280 + 5760 + 960 + 80 = 45726\n  \\]\n  This is not equal to 41.\n\n- **\\( b = 13 \\):**\n  \\[\n  13^4 + 10 \\times 13^3 + 40 \\times 13^2 + 80 \\times 13 + 80 = 28561 + 21970 + 6760 + 1040 + 80 = 58411\n  \\]\n  This is not equal to 41.\n\n- **\\( b = 14 \\):**\n  \\[\n  14^4 + 10 \\times 14^3 + 40 \\times 14^2 + 80 \\times 14 + 80 = 38416 + 27440 + 7840 + 1120 + 80 = 75896\n  \\]\n  This is not equal to 41.\n\n- **\\( b = 15 \\):**\n  \\[\n  15^4 + 10 \\times 15^3 + 40 \\times 15^2 + 80 \\times 15 + 80 = 50625 + 33750 + 9000 + 1200 + 80 = 94655\n  \\]\n  This is not equal to 41.\n\n- **\\( b = 16 \\):**\n  \\[\n  16^4 + 10 \\times 16^3 + 40 \\times 16^2 + 80 \\times 16 + 80 = 65536 + 40960 + 10240 + 1280 + 80 = 117096\n  \\]\n  This is not equal to 41.\n\n- **\\( b = 17 \\):**\n  \\[\n  17^4 + 10 \\times 17^3 + 40 \\times 17^2 + 80 \\times 17 + 80 = 83521 + 49130 + 11560 + 1360 + 80 = 145651\n  \\]\n  This is not equal to 41.\n\n- **\\( b = 18 \\):**\n  \\[\n  18^4 + 10 \\times 18^3 + 40 \\times 18^2 + 80 \\times 18 + 80 = 104976 + 58320 + 12960 + 1440 + 80 = 177776\n  \\]\n  This is not equal to 41.\n\n- **\\( b = 19 \\):**\n  \\[\n  19^4 + 10 \\times 19^3 + 40 \\times 19^2 + 80 \\times 19 + 80 = 130321 + 68590 + 14480 + 1520 + 80 = 214991\n  \\]\n  This is not equal to 41.\n\n- **\\( b = 20 \\):**\n  \\[\n  20^4 + 10 \\times 20^3 + 40 \\times 20^2 + 80 \\times 20 + 80 = 160000 + 80000 + 16000 + 1600 + 80 = 257680\n  \\]\n  This is not equal to 41.\n\n### Step 6: Conclusion\nThe largest base \\( b \\) such that the sum of the digits of \\( 12^5 \\) in base \\( b \\) is not equal to 41 is \\( b = 20 \\).\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{20}\n\\]",
